index a096fdeaa7887dacb1a4d37aa15f76c4236763e6..27b6a40d261d42d45cbf115d7b7778c3629ecdcd 100644
--- a/docs/cli.rst
+++ b/docs/cli.rst
@@ -744,6 +744,16 @@ This also means you pipe ``sqlite-utils`` together to easily create a new SQLite
     $ sqlite-utils sf-trees.db \
         "select TreeID, qAddress, Latitude, Longitude from Street_Tree_List" --nl \
       | sqlite-utils insert saved.db trees - --nl
+
+You can use ``--convert`` to run Python code against each incoming object before
+it is inserted. The object is available as ``row`` and can be modified in
+place. Every input object will still be inserted::
+
+    $ echo '{"n": "1"}' | sqlite-utils insert numbers.db numbers - \
+        --convert 'row["n"] = int(row["n"]) + 1'
+
+The :mod:`sqlite_utils.recipes` module is available to conversion code as both
+``r`` and ``recipes``.
     # This creates saved.db with a single table called trees:
     $ sqlite-utils saved.db "select * from trees limit 5" --csv
     TreeID,qAddress,Latitude,Longitude
